---
import {services} from '../../../data/site';
import {VOICES,CHECKS,emptyDraft,type Draft} from '../../../lib/content-studio/model';
import {pagePerformanceEvidence} from '../../../lib/seo-review-dashboard';
import SeoContentPerformance from '../SeoContentPerformance.astro';
import {when} from '../../../lib/admin-data';
import '../../../styles/content-studio.css';
interface Props {snapshot?:any; documents:Draft[]; inventory:{slug:string;title:string;author:string;service:string;body:string}[]; storageError?:string}
const {snapshot,documents,inventory,storageError=''}=Astro.props;
const performance=pagePerformanceEvidence(snapshot?[snapshot.data]:[]);
const starter=emptyDraft();
const state={starter,inventory,documents,checks:CHECKS};
const safeJson=JSON.stringify(state).replace(/</g,'\\u003c');
---
<div class="cs" id="content-studio" data-studio>
 <div class="cs-intro"><p>Research with evidence. Write with character. Publish with confidence.</p><span class="cs-state">Private working drafts · publication stays separate</span></div>
 <nav class="cs-tabs" aria-label="Content Studio"><button type="button" data-panel="overview" aria-pressed="true">Performance</button><button type="button" data-panel="pillars">Pillars</button><button type="button" data-panel="ranks">Rank tracking</button><button type="button" data-panel="brief">Research &amp; brief</button><button type="button" data-panel="write">Writing desk</button><button type="button" data-panel="review">Review &amp; resources</button></nav>
 <p class="cs-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-status></p>
 <section data-view="overview"><div class="cs-section-head"><div><p class="a-label">Your publishing system</p><h2>Know what earns attention.</h2></div><button class="a-button primary" type="button" data-refresh>Refresh Google metrics</button></div>
 <div class="cs-summary"><div><span>Published articles</span><strong>{inventory.length}</strong><small>Current public content inventory</small></div><div><span>Service pillars</span><strong>{services.length}</strong><small>One primary service per article</small></div><div><span>Studio drafts</span><strong>{documents.length}</strong><small>Up to 200 most recent working drafts</small></div><div><span>Evidence refreshed</span><strong class="cs-date">{snapshot?when(snapshot.measuredAt):'Not collected'}</strong><small>{snapshot?'GA4 '+snapshot.property+' · GSC '+snapshot.searchProperty:'Connect sources in Backend'}</small></div></div>
 {storageError&&<p class="a-error">{storageError}</p>}
 <SeoContentPerformance evidence={performance?[performance]:[]} basePath="/admin/content-studio/"/>
 <details class="cs-help"><summary>Other measurements and interpretation</summary><p>Article views, total foreground engagement seconds, search clicks, impressions, matching-period changes and article-to-service referrer views are included above. CTR and query positions are in Rank tracking. Service referrals are not unique visitors or qualified leads. Search Console does not separate Google AI-feature traffic. AI citations, fixed-location rankings, revenue attribution and qualified inquiries require their own source evidence and are not inferred from traffic.</p><a class="a-link" href="/admin/analysis/">Open existing analysis and inquiry-funnel evidence</a></details></section>
 <section data-view="pillars" hidden><p class="a-label">Coverage &amp; commercial relevance</p><h2>Build depth around the right services.</h2><p class="a-muted">The category organizes the articles. Its substantive overview explains the topic and links to supporting guides. Article count measures coverage volume, not authority or quality.</p><div class="cs-pillar-grid">{services.map(s=>{const posts=inventory.filter(p=>p.service===s.slug),measured=performance?.pillars.find(p=>p.slug===s.slug);return <article><div class="cs-pillar-title"><h3>{s.title}</h3><strong>{posts.length}</strong></div><p class="a-count">{posts.length===1?'published article':'published articles'}</p><p><a href={'/blog/category/'+s.slug+'/'} class="a-link">Category overview</a> · <a href={'/services/'+s.slug+'/'} class="a-link">Service</a></p><p>Observed article-to-service views: <strong>{measured?.serviceReferrals?.current??'Unavailable'}</strong></p><details><summary>Inspect coverage</summary><ul>{posts.map(p=><li><button type="button" class="cs-text-button" data-open-article={p.slug}>{p.title}</button></li>)}</ul>{!posts.length&&<p>No published article is assigned to this service.</p>}</details><button class="a-button" type="button" data-plan-service={s.slug}>Research a topic</button></article>;})}</div></section>
 <section data-view="ranks" hidden><p class="a-label">Native Search Console observations</p><h2>Follow queries and position changes.</h2><p class="a-muted">Matched 28-day periods, final web data, all devices and countries. These are observed average positions, not fixed-location Miami or Panama City ranks.</p><div class="cs-controls"><label class="a-field">Article<select class="a-input" data-rank-article>{inventory.map(p=><option value={p.slug}>{p.title}</option>)}</select></label><button class="a-button" type="button" data-saved-ranks>Read saved report</button><button class="a-button" type="button" data-rank-history>History</button><button class="a-button primary" type="button" data-ranks>Refresh query positions</button></div><div data-rank-results><p>No article selected for measurement yet.</p></div></section>
 <div class="cs-working" data-work-controls hidden><label class="a-field">Working document<select class="a-input" data-document><option value="">New draft</option>{documents.map(d=><option value={d.slug}>{d.title||d.slug} · v{d.revision}</option>)}</select></label><label class="a-field">Draft identifier<input class="a-input" data-field="slug" value="new-article" pattern="[a-z0-9-]+" maxlength="150"/></label><button class="a-button primary" type="button" data-save>Save private draft</button><span class="a-count" data-revision>Unsaved</span></div>
 <section data-view="brief" hidden><div class="cs-section-head"><div><p class="a-label">Audience → evidence → topic</p><h2>Decide what deserves an article.</h2></div><a class="a-button" href="/admin/research/">Research library</a></div>
 <div class="cs-brief-grid"><label class="a-field">Working title<input class="a-input" data-field="title" maxlength="10000"/></label><label class="a-field">Primary service<select class="a-input" data-field="service">{services.map(s=><option value={s.slug} selected={s.slug==='seo'}>{s.title}</option>)}</select></label><label class="a-field">Author<select class="a-input" data-field="author"><option value="">Choose an author explicitly</option>{Object.entries(VOICES).map(([key,v])=><option value={key} selected={key==='wendy'}>{v.name} · {v.role}</option>)}</select></label><label class="a-field">Format<select class="a-input" data-field="format">{['How-to','Comprehensive guide','Deep dive','Industry analysis','Comparison'].map(v=><option>{v}</option>)}</select></label><label class="a-field">Target reader and situation<textarea class="a-input" data-field="audience" rows="3">Business owner</textarea></label><label class="a-field">Search intent<textarea class="a-input" data-field="intent" rows="3">Learn how</textarea></label><label class="a-field">The specific question<textarea class="a-input" data-field="question" rows="3"/></label><label class="a-field">What this adds beyond existing coverage<textarea class="a-input" data-field="contribution" rows="3"/></label></div>
 <label class="a-field">Research, supporting URLs, claims, dates and limitations<textarea class="a-input" data-field="research" rows="8" placeholder="Record what each source supports, when it was checked, and unresolved questions. Private experience needs approved provenance."/></label><label class="a-field">Pillar overview, supporting articles and intended links<textarea class="a-input" data-field="links" rows="4" placeholder="Name each destination and why the reader needs it. Preserve the existing service/category."/></label>
 <p class="a-muted">Every request includes the saved article inventory and native performance snapshot with its periods and gaps. Add current primary-source research before writing. Site impressions are not total market demand.</p><button class="a-button" type="button" data-assist="research">Claude · analyze topic opportunity</button></section>
 <section data-view="write" hidden><div class="cs-editor-grid"><aside class="cs-voice"><p class="a-label">Author direction</p>{Object.entries(VOICES).map(([key,v])=><div data-voice={key} hidden={key!=='wendy'}><h3>{v.name}</h3><p>{v.description}</p></div>)}<p class="a-count">US English · natural paragraphs</p><p>The named author determines voice. No rigid paragraph rules, invented experiences or detector-immunity claims.</p></aside><div class="cs-manuscript"><label class="a-field">TL;DR<textarea class="a-input" data-field="tldr" rows="4"/></label><label class="a-field">Full manuscript · Markdown<textarea class="a-input cs-body" data-field="body" rows="24" placeholder="The complete article belongs here. Saving cannot publish it."/></label><div class="cs-controls"><button class="a-button primary" type="button" data-assist="write">GPT · propose a full draft</button><button class="a-button" type="button" data-export>Download manuscript</button></div></div></div></section>
 <section data-view="review" hidden><div class="cs-section-head"><div><p class="a-label">Evidence before approval</p><h2>Check the whole reader experience.</h2></div><div class="cs-gauge"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 60" role="img" aria-label="Review completion"><path d="M10 50 A40 40 0 0 1 90 50" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" opacity=".15" stroke-width="8"/><path data-gauge d="M10 50 A40 40 0 0 1 90 50" pathLength="100" fill="none" stroke="var(--tealt)" stroke-width="8" stroke-dasharray="0 100"/></svg><strong data-progress>0 / 16</strong><small>Documented checks, not an SEO score</small></div></div>
 <label class="a-field">Artwork and reader downloads · URLs, purpose and verification notes<textarea class="a-input" data-field="resources" rows="5" placeholder="Hero + topic-specific explanatory graphic. Check exact logos, white mugs, labels, alt text, dimensions, social crops. For files: actual download/open, PDF text/links/forms save/reopen, spreadsheet formulas and specimen data."/></label><div class="cs-brief-grid"><label class="a-field">Search title<input class="a-input" data-field="metaTitle"/></label><label class="a-field">Search description<textarea class="a-input" data-field="description" rows="3"/></label></div>
 <p class="a-notice">Changing the manuscript, brief, resources or metadata resets all checks. Pass means you have evidence for this version; a model response does not approve it. Publication is not available from this workspace.</p>
 <div class="cs-controls"><button class="a-button" type="button" data-inspect="draft">Inspect draft structure</button><button class="a-button" type="button" data-inspect="public">Inspect existing public SEO</button></div><div data-inspection></div><div class="cs-checks">{Object.entries(CHECKS).map(([id,label])=><div class="cs-check"><label>{label}<select class="a-input" data-check={id}><option value="pending">Pending</option><option value="pass">Pass · evidence required</option><option value="fail">Needs correction</option><option value="not-applicable">Exception requested · blocks handoff</option></select></label><label class="a-field"><span class="a-count">Evidence or reason</span><textarea class="a-input" data-evidence={id} rows="2" maxlength="3000"/></label></div>)}</div><div class="cs-controls"><button class="a-button" type="button" data-assist="review">Claude · challenge this draft</button><button class="a-button" type="button" data-history>View saved versions</button></div><div data-history-results></div><div class="cs-review-comments"><h3>Review comments</h3><label class="a-field">Comment on this saved version<textarea class="a-input" rows="3" maxlength="8000" data-review-comment/></label><div class="cs-controls"><button class="a-button" type="button" data-add-comment>Save comment</button><button class="a-button" type="button" data-read-comments>Read comments</button><button class="a-button" type="button" data-handoff>Export reviewed release package</button></div><p class="a-count">Owner-only handoff after every check passes. Exception requests block handoff. Export does not publish. Article-specific holds remain enforced.</p><div data-comments></div></div></section>
 <section class="cs-assistance" hidden data-assistance><div class="cs-section-head"><h2>Assistant proposal</h2><button class="a-button" type="button" data-check-job>Check request</button></div><p class="a-count" data-job-status>No request started.</p><pre data-result></pre><button class="a-button" type="button" data-apply hidden>Use proposed manuscript · unsaved</button></section>
 <footer class="cs-footer"><span>Content Studio · existing staff access</span><span>Wendy’s article-cluster rewrite: owner review hold</span></footer>
</div>
<script type="application/json" id="content-studio-state" set:html={safeJson}/>
<script>import '../../../scripts/admin/content-studio';</script>
